      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'm also wondering about the specific wording regarding the \"unforeseeable\" nature of these events. Sometimes these regulatory shifts occur because of underlying chaos or unexpected interference in the administrative process. If we were to argue that the disruption was caused by something essentially capricious or \"hidden\" from the parties' view—almost like a sudden, inexplicable breakdown in the expected logic of the system—how would that affect the \"beyond control\" argument?",
