      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When an event is capricious or an \"inexplicable breakdown\" in the administrative process, it leans strongly into the realm of a true, unforeseeable event. This points toward a systemic failure or a governmental action so arbitrary it qualifies as beyond reasonable foresight. Arguing this helps bolster the \"beyond control\" element because it suggests the disruption originated from chaotic external forces rather than anticipated business volatility. Such situations provide the strongest basis for claiming the event is not merely a foreseeable, albeit difficult, market fluctuation.",
